Give Haiku a DriveMetricsProvider::HasSeekPenalty().

`components/metrics/BUILD.gn` drops `drive_metrics_provider_linux.cc` on Haiku
-- correctly, it reads `/sys/block` -- and puts nothing in its place, which
leaves `DriveMetricsProvider::HasSeekPenalty()` undefined. That has been true
since the file was first excluded and nobody noticed, because `--gc-sections`
discards the section holding the reference before BFD ld has to resolve
anything, and this build has never linked without `--gc-sections`.

lld resolves symbols before it collects sections, so it says so:

	ld.lld: error: undefined symbol:
	  metrics::DriveMetricsProvider::HasSeekPenalty(base::FilePath const&, bool*)
	>>> referenced by metrics_jumbo_2.cc
	>>>   metrics/metrics_jumbo_2.o:(...GetDriveMetricsOnBackgroundThread(int))

Fuchsia's file is exactly the stub this wants -- report "no seek penalty, and
that answer is known" -- and Haiku already takes several other Fuchsia files
for the same reason (idle_fuchsia.cc, select_file_dialog_fuchsia.cc). Nothing
on this port reads the metric; content_shell has no metrics upload.

--- a/components/metrics/BUILD.gn
+++ b/components/metrics/BUILD.gn
@@ -194,6 +194,7 @@
   if (is_haiku) {
     sources -= [ "drive_metrics_provider_linux.cc" ]
+    sources += [ "drive_metrics_provider_fuchsia.cc" ]
   }
 }
